data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Adding x with count n: delta = x - mean, mean += delta / n, M2 += delta * (x - mean_new). Removing the\nvalue old from a window of n values: mean_new = mean + (mean - old) / (n - 1), and M2 -= (old - mean_new)\n* (old - mean). The sample standard deviation is sqrt(M2 / (n - 1)). Centre the values first by\nsubtracting a reference value near the data, then add it back to the means. A large common offset\notherwise costs digits over a long series. Rescale deviations before squaring at extreme magnitudes; rescale the running mean and M2 consistently."},"hints_note":null}

